{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1190095-help-me-with-evocations-for-shapeshifting-smashfists","id":1190095,"title":"Help me with Evocations for shapeshifting smashfists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-27T19:03:27-08:00","id":1190095,"title":"Help me with Evocations for shapeshifting smashfists","content":"So I had an idea for Moonsilver Smashfists that I needed some help with fleshing out the evocations for. The ultimate idea is that the Smashfists come to life and can act on their own accord, so the first charm in the tree (or rather the second) would operate very similarly to the form charm from Single Point style. The imagery for the gauntlets themselves was that they were meant to look like ravenous maws of some kind of beast and the first charm you unlock for free I designed was called Feed the Fangs, basically you can spend 1-2 motes during a decisive attack to convert lethal damage dealt into Blood Motes that are stored in the Artifact. This secondary resource would then be used to activate and maintain the various charms in the tree.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo with that in mind, as I said the second charm would allow the gauntlets to come to life, transforming into a ravenous beast made of Moonsilver and glowing with the essence of whatever type of Exalt wields it. Despite the thematic the creature would still act as if it were delivering attacks from you (using Brawl) it would just act on its own initiative and you would lose the benefits of wearing the gauntlets. The idea is that the charms would augment or supplement this core mechanic while progressively making you more like the beast as you progress until reaching the capstone charm which allows you to fuse with the beast and get a sort of War form from it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAny of you more knowledgeable people think you could help out with coming up with some charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1983-einlanzer","name":"Einlanzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1983_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:37:55-08:00","id":1190109,"title":"","content":"Without writing up specifics, it sounds like you're crossing Lion-O's gauntlet with the skilled use of the Bigby's Hands range of classic spells. <br /> <br /> Perhaps your smashfists could ...<br /> <br /> Add a bonus to grapple based on the strength in the jaw-fingers and the grabbiness of the fang-claws. <br /> <br /> Detach to guard you, gaining a pool a bit like Single Point's charge, except that it joins with its master to grapple. Why grab two limbs when you can grab all four? <br /> <br /> Join with you to grab and lift things, helping you move large loads or perform feats of strength.<br /> <br /> At a higher level, manifest the full monstrous body, either of liquid moonsilver or white fire or smoke or gears or a cloud of silk or whatever. <br /> <br /> Improve the manifest to function as a mount with great strength, such as also benefits large-scale Crafting (castles, manses, etc)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:03:02-07:00","id":1211777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1190095-help-me-with-evocations-for-shapeshifting-smashfists?p=1190109#post1190109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without writing up specifics, it sounds like you're crossing Lion-O's gauntlet with the skilled use of the Bigby's Hands range of classic spells.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your smashfists could ...<br /> <br /> Add a bonus to grapple based on the strength in the jaw-fingers and the grabbiness of the fang-claws.<br /> <br /> Detach to guard you, gaining a pool a bit like Single Point's charge, except that it joins with its master to grapple. Why grab two limbs when you can grab all four?<br /> <br /> Join with you to grab and lift things, helping you move large loads or perform feats of strength.<br /> <br /> At a higher level, manifest the full monstrous body, either of liquid moonsilver or white fire or smoke or gears or a cloud of silk or whatever.<br /> <br /> Improve the manifest to function as a mount with great strength, such as also benefits large-scale Crafting (castles, manses, etc)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically the general idea I had in mind. The idea behind the gauntlets was that I wanted them to in a way also serve as an Artifact Familiar, but also embody the characters raw primal fighting style as well. The problem is, while I can easily come up with ideas for different charms in the tree I'm not great at the crunchy bits and not sure how to stat them in a way that would be balanced and fun.<br /> <br /> Some ideas I had like I mentioned in the original post were like a Charm that allows the wielder to convert damage from decisive attacks into Blood Motes, a charm called Feeding the Fangs or something along those lines. From that point on them, the Evocations would have a cost of something like (3m, 1bm) or something along those lines. In truth the idea was sort of inspired by two Artifacts from Arms of the Chosen; Stormcaller which generates wind points effectively as the wielder fights, and Mela's Coil which eventually transforms the wearer into a Dragon. The idea behind this was that I wanted the smashfists to give charms that would let the wielder emulate a beast, as well as eventually becoming the weapons eventually becoming the beast itself.<br /> <br /> Single Point was another inspiration with the idea of eventually granted the smashfists their own initiative track as they start to operate on their own, biting and gnawing at enemies locked in combat with the wielder and stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1983-einlanzer","name":"Einlanzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1983_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}